# 🌦️ Mini Project — SkyCast Weather App

## Project Overview

SkyCast is a responsive weather application built using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript. It retrieves weather information for a city and displays current conditions and a seven-day forecast.

## Features

- Search weather by city name
- Current temperature
- Feels-like temperature
- Relative humidity
- Wind speed
- Weather condition descriptions and icons
- Local date and day/night information
- Seven-day forecast cards
- Input validation and loading messages
- API error handling
- Responsive layout

## Technologies

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Vanilla JavaScript
- Fetch API
- Promises and `.then()` / `.catch()`
- DOM manipulation
- Open-Meteo Geocoding API
- Open-Meteo Forecast API
- Git and GitHub

## API Endpoints

**Geocoding API**

Converts the city name into latitude and longitude.

```text
https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search
```

**Weather Forecast API**

Returns current weather and daily forecast data.

```text
https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
```

No API key is required for this project. An internet connection is needed to retrieve data.

Weather data: [Open-Meteo](https://open-meteo.com/)

## Project Structure

```text
8-week-roadmap/
├── week2.js
